            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54911",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "UltraJSON is a fast JSON encoder and decoder written in pure C with bi ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "UltraJSON is a fast JSON encoder and decoder written in pure C with bindings for Python 3.7+. Prior to 5.13.0, ujson.dumps() (or ujson.dump() or ujson.encode()) have a reject_bytes=False option. When set, they may accept malformed or truncated UTF-8 byte sequences, silently rewriting them into different Unicode characters instead of rejecting them. This leads to input validation bypass and data integrity issues. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.13.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54911",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54911\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: ujson\nFixed Version: 5.13.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-54911](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54911)\nUltraJSON is a fast JSON encoder and decoder written in pure C with bindings for Python 3.7+. Prior to 5.13.0, ujson.dumps() (or ujson.dump() or ujson.encode()) have a reject_bytes=False option. When set, they may accept malformed or truncated UTF-8 byte sequences, silently rewriting them into different Unicode characters instead of rejecting them. This leads to input validation bypass and data integrity issues. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.13.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54911**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|ujson|5.13.0|[CVE-2026-54911](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54911)|\n\nUltraJSON is a fast JSON encoder and decoder written in pure C with bindings for Python 3.7+. Prior to 5.13.0, ujson.dumps() (or ujson.dump() or ujson.encode()) have a reject_bytes=False option. When set, they may accept malformed or truncated UTF-8 byte sequences, silently rewriting them into different Unicode characters instead of rejecting them. This leads to input validation bypass and data integrity issues. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.13.0."
              },
